  "limitations": [
    "D034 (owner rule 2026-10-18): this chunk completes at 8/10 with no blockers; it is raised to 9/10 before the P03 phase review. C09 completed at 8/8/8/8/8; its review's R1-R3, E1 and the core part of E2 are remediated in this tree (docs/planning/reviews/C09/follow-ups.md: one-shot secret reveal with SecretState::Shown, expiry re-checked at confirmation via CoreConfig::review_lifetime, atomic consume-and-admit with ChangeFailure::Capacity, a captured draft ending a pending confirmation, exact request/readback tests for every remaining supported Runtime operation) and are re-reviewed as C09 at the P03 push. C08's R1-R3/E1 fixes landed with C09.",
    "D036 (decisions.md) and the DESIGN C10 section record the DLP capability table (exactly v1's protocol.ts matrix; no filtering-profile create/delete, no data-profile delete, no merge-patch; deployment profiles and the AIRS DLP catalog read-only), DLP baselines and readback by each item's own get, no authorship on DLP writes (v1), v1's validDataProfile ported exactly, dictionary bodies and the SDK multipart upload, and staged keyword files.",
    "v1 entered dictionary keywords only as text; C10's milestone asks for native file selection, so a dictionary may also use a file chosen in a native sheet (rfd/NSOpenPanel in production; the fixture build answers with a file the driver staged in its data root). Rust reads it once (256 KiB read bound; UTF-8, byte-order mark dropped, non-empty, <= 64 Ki UTF-16 units), never writes it, and stages it under a random token for the active context; drafts reference it as fileRef and the renderer never sees a path or the content.",
    "No real DLP endpoint was called. dlp_subset (7 tests) runs against a stateful synthetic TLS service with an independent RFC 7578 reader asserting the literal multipart parts (names, file names, content types, exact bytes, the scm-sdk boundary); native acceptance runs against tools/native-acceptance/mgmt_server.py, now with stateful DLP collections and multipart logging by part SHA-256 (it keeps C08's one-item-per-page data-pattern listing so C08's Spring paging regression still holds).",
    "The academy_offline test a_downloaded_course_is_kept_sealed_for_its_account_under_academys_lease asserted the offline state immediately after sign-in and flaked once under a loaded parallel run; it now waits for that state (no behavior change).",
    "Because the change workbench, Administration and the authority grew, C01-C09 native acceptance were re-run as regressions on the C10 bundle (docs/planning/evidence/C10/native-acceptance-C0x.json and native-regressions/).",
    "Mutation probes: docs/planning/evidence/C10/mutation-probes (allowed matrix, data-profile legacy field and structure rules, dictionary bounds and file names, staged-token binding, staged size and byte-order mark, DLP readback, the 204 dictionary replace, the presentation's file reference and per-inventory actions, staged-token contract validation; baselines pass).",
    "The C09 native driver was restructured for C09's one-shot reveal (R1): a key is shown once and no longer offered, so sheet expiry, Clear key and the foreign-clipboard case each use their own key; C09-N06/N07's descriptions were updated to match. The first C10 chain's C09 regression failed three times on the old driver expecting a second reveal (retained in the run log).",
    "tools/native-acceptance/mgmt_server.py now gives applications created by a key create a tsg_id (the SDK's application list model requires it, as the real service supplies); without it a second key creation's application check decoded as an invalid reply.",
    "C09's one-shot reveal (R1 remediation) did not publish the changed state: RevealSecret now calls changed(), so the presentation stops offering a reveal the core would refuse. The C09 native regression on the C10 bundle found it (C09-N06 'no longer offered' failed three times); runtime_changes now asserts the published update and a C09 probe guards it. The C10 bundle was rebuilt and every native record re-run on it."
